  <static seed="1756" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicAlgebra/SignedNumbersArithemtic/MultiplyWithNegativeIntegers20.pg">
    <statement><p>Multiply the following.
<ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>(-2)\cdot(-5)\cdot(-2)</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>5\cdot(-9)\cdot(-1)</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>(-89)\cdot(-54)\cdot0</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-20</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>45</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>a.</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}[t]
        (-2)\cdot(-5)\cdot(-2) \amp  = 10\cdot(-2) \\
                                     \amp  = {-20}
       \end{aligned}</m></p>
<p>b.</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}[t]
         5\cdot(-9)\cdot(-1) \amp  = -45\cdot(-1)  \\
                       \amp  = {45}  
       \end{aligned}</m></p>
<p>c.</p>
<p><m>-89\cdot(-54)\cdot0 =0</m></p>
<p>Note that in the last case there is no need to waste time multiplying the first two numbers because any number multiplied by <m>0</m> equals <m>0</m>.</p>
</solution>
